' plan-114-D: a record field carries the SAME two `RES`-marker rules a collection
' element does, because it is the same kind of slot -- one that may hold a handle
' pointer (spec 15.6). This fixture pins the second of the pair.
'
' `RES` marks ownership of a RESOURCE. Putting it on a data type is not a
' harmless decoration: it would claim the field holds a handle whose close
' obligation floats to the record's scope, so the escape analysis would try to
' drain an Integer as if it were a resource. Rejected with
' TYPE_RES_REQUIRES_RESOURCE, exactly as `List OF RES Integer` is.
'
' The twin fixture resource-record-field-invalid pins the other direction: a
' resource field with the marker MISSING.
IMPORT io

TYPE Holder
  count AS RES Integer
END TYPE

FUNC main AS Integer
  io::print("unreachable")
  RETURN 0
END FUNC
